Update z.function() type to support array input (#5170)

* Update z.function() type to support array input

It is documented to work with array inputs like:

```
const myFunction = z.function({
  input: [z.object({
    name: z.string(),
    age: z.number().int(),
  })],
  output: z.string(),
});

myFunction.implement((input) => {
  return `Hello ${input.name}, you are ${input.age} years old.`;
});
```

But it doesn't work. Current type only support `z.tuple()`.

* Tweak

---------

